{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779397787,"nonce":"C2aqhj2U03hFxhRjXbWwyGSlG+M=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDBj8sQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/152","origin":"github"},"title":"Rear camera over VPN — enable for OTH / Starlink-path situational awareness","message":"## Problem\n\nSurfaced from 2026-05-21 deployment debrief: the bizzy rear camera is currently not reachable on the VPN / Starlink path — useful for backing-down operations, post-collision situational awareness, and \"what's behind me\" checks during recovery. Operationally important during the 2026-05-21 incident: after the collision, the operator was driving with the USB controller toward dock without a rear view through the VPN-only link to Ruby's pursuit position.\n\n## Task\n\n- [ ] Confirm current state of the rear-camera stream: which topic(s), which bridge config (WiFi-only? operator-side reachable but not on the topic stream that crosses Starlink/VPN?). Source-verify rather than guess — `bizzyboat_project11/launch/` and the `udp_bridge` config in `bizzyboat.yaml` are the likely places.\n- [ ] Identify the change needed to bring the rear camera through the VPN/Starlink path. Likely options:\n  - Add the rear-camera topic to the boat→operator bridge topic list, possibly at a lower frame rate / quality preset for the VPN-path budget.\n  - If the topic is already bridged but at a quality that gets dropped on lossy paths: tune for VPN-friendly bitrate, separate from the WiFi-path config.\n- [ ] Apply, smoke-test in a bench / dockside setup, and field-validate on next OTH or VPN-only segment.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Topic budget on Starlink-only is already tight (the 2026-05-21 OTH segment ended on collision before bandwidth-saturation analysis could complete — see [`#150 topic 3`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/150)). Rear camera should land as a *low-priority, low-bandwidth* stream — operator wants it for occasional reference, not for sustained navigation.\n- Coordinate with the keyframe-tuning work in [`#151`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/151) — both touch the OAK encoder config; doing them together avoids round-tripping.\n\n## Why now\n\nLake Massabesic surveys go OTH routinely from a shore-based operator. Backing-down maneuvers and \"what's behind me\" reference during student-led ops are class-relevant.\n\n## References\n\n- Source debrief: 2026-05-21 dev log entry around 17:05 EDT, [`unh_echoboats_project11#149`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/149).\n- Related: [`#151`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/151) (keyframe tuning).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}